      "quote": "## SP2-LOCAL-FOUNDATION-001\n\n- Grant date: 2026-10-19, effective on owner installation. Grantor and accountable owner: project owner (decision verbatim in evidence/owner_rulings_2026-10-19/sp1_exit_sp2/DECISION_VERBATIM.txt SHA-256 6332dca82d347b3d2bf83b7190fcb529786bff0f07895746757b47ae4eeb1852: \"Also localnet launches now\"; \"Move into start/\"). Executors: Codex and Claude, with producer and non-producer roles disclosed per deliverable.\n- Machine: the current local machine, observed hostname `strix`. No remote runner or cloud resources.\n- Programme: fresh `NewArc/3m` only; SP2 of Plan \u00a74.2 L412 under the approved v4.2.8 working plan and its exact manifest. Working tracker: RWA/start/DRWA_SP2_Task_Tracker.md, placed there by this installation from the draft RWA/DRWA_SP2_Task_Tracker.md SHA-256 935cb2c1a6f2b0ba53e61d62f98251bba24210bfba165154fea17fddbe35750a; rows are taken in the dependency order of Plan \u00a74.4. Existing excluded work and unselected platform repositories remain excluded.\n- Expiry: end of SP2 or revocation, whichever occurs first. No automatic SP3, architecture-freeze or production-stage authority.\n- Permitted local development: after each row's source, model, authority and first-consumer prerequisites are satisfied, make SP2 source and test changes within the bound repository inventory and the row's plan work area; use adequate upstream facilities. Explicitly non-normative experiments may explore alternatives under Part A C.4; they cannot earn conforming model or profile acceptance.\n- Permitted execution: local offline builds, unit/integration/race/fuzz/static/benchmark checks and in-process test helpers, plus necessary read-only package dependency downloads to bounded caches. Smoke-check exact commands first. No public-network tests or upstream workflow execution. Inherited upstream packages run with `-short` unless the exact suite and configuration were inspected first. Test-owned temporary upstream integration tests, including multi-node libp2p tests and in-process chain-simulator tests, are permitted only with loopback-only network endpoints, bounded temporary state, and cleanup of every test-owned listener/process; no public-network or non-loopback access.\n- Permitted localnet launches (contract \u00a711): launching the SP2-13 localnet on this machine \u2014 seednode, validators, observers and proxy in one tmux session, MultiversX TermUI against the shard-1 observer in a second \u2014 only from an execution package with its own recorded identity, with every listener bound to loopback, local-only peer lists and no public network, MultiversX network, gateway or public API access (contract \u00a75). Every operational step (preflight, launch, health check, capture, shutdown) is a smoke-tested script with its SHA-256 recorded (contract \u00a78). Retain `tmux list-sessions`, both pane identities, the TermUI command and binary SHA-256 and a successful shard-1 status response; shut down through the operator entrypoint and confirm that no package-owned process remains. A changed package needs a new identity before it runs again.\n- Stagecheck: Codex and Claude may each invoke `stagecheck/bin/stagecheck.sh` in delivery mode, `--depth code`, all checks report-only and model agents off, for their own SP2 delivery and audit records. No stagecheck configuration change.\n- Prerequisites remain binding: affected expected-model acceptance waits for its independent review; first-consumer constructions are not waived. No arbitrary numeric defaults outside R7 (line 64), unsupported profile or new protocol semantics may be adopted; novel protocol, VM, gas, storage, P2P, cryptographic, transaction or shard behaviour still needs owner approval (contract \u00a75).\n- Excluded: signing and pushes, repository creation on GitHub, PRs/issues/comments, deployment, any public or MultiversX network, transaction submission (including to the localnet), fault injection, runtime or stage acceptance, architecture freeze, production-format freeze, release and qualification-file cleanup. A new bounded grant is required for those operations.\n- Evidence: retain exact inputs/commands/exits/results under the bound evidence root. Agents may update only the enumerated factual state fields under the installed instruction files' current-state update rule. Protected state fields, grants and acceptance remain owner-only. Completed tasks do not constitute sprint acceptance. Preserve before/after state bytes and append a linked update record under the evidence root. No producer can assign its own independent acceptance."
    },
